    "gp_section_604839635750880061": {
      "type": "gp-section-604839635750880061",
      "settings": {
        "checksum": "397276169b1f0a33031f075985379d60084ee42b105ffb0ebc10360cf9b44678_1_1_1_0__1",
        "ggPTQ4b2Oyp_text": "<strong>Ear scratching today. </strong><span style=\"color:#D62020;\"><strong>Infections tomorrow.</strong></span>",
        "ggUD4YdXUjF_text": "<p>That scratching and head shaking you see every day? It's not just an itch.</p><p>That's bacteria and yeast building up in the warm, moist ear canal. And when it sits there day after day, here's what happens:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Days 1-7: </strong>Bacteria multiplies. Your dog scratches more frequently, introducing even more bacteria from their paws.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Weeks 2-3:</strong> The scratching gets worse. Redness and inflammation appear. That corn chip smell becomes stronger.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Week 4+</strong>: What started as mild discomfort turns into painful inflammation. Left untreated, this leads to infections requiring $300+ vet visits.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The problem isn't that you're ignoring it. The problem is that most cleaning methods make it worse.</p>",
        "gg7zWXq-7qs_text": "<p><i><strong>Most dog owners try 3-5 different products before finding one that actually works</strong></i></p>"
      }
    },
    "gp_section_604839635750945597": {
      "type": "gp-section-604839635750945597",
      "settings": {
